"""Current feature guides. Shared by the generated docs and their search index."""
UPDATES={
'':'''<div class="callout tip"><p>Current release: <b>0.14.1</b>. Instant Replay now includes desktop audio. Start with the setup guide, or explore what is new.</p></div><h2 id="start">Make yourself at home</h2><p>Larp Client is a visual and utility mod for Minecraft 1.21.11 on Fabric. It brings together 3D cosmetics, a movable HUD, world effects and tools for everyday play.</p><div class="cards-doc"><a href="/docs/installation"><b>Install Larp</b><span>Requirements, private access and updating.</span></a><a href="/docs/modules"><b>Explore the modules</b><span>All {module_count} registered modules and their settings.</span></a><a href="/docs/instant-replay"><b>Keep your last 30 seconds</b><span>Clips with audio, saved manually or after a kill.</span></a><a href="/docs/kill-effects"><b>Kill Efects</b><span>Tralalero, Samurai and in-menu previews.</span></a></div><h2 id="first-session">Your first session</h2><p>Open the client menu with <kbd>Right Shift</kbd>. Enable what you want, customize your HUD and save a profile. Most effects are optional; start small and add to your setup.</p><h2 id="website-previews">About the website previews</h2><p>The screenshots and cosmetic renders are actual client assets. Interactive website controls are illustrative browser demos. They do not run Minecraft, change your client configuration or create real clips.</p>''',
'installation':'''<h2 id="requirements">Before you start</h2><ul><li>Minecraft <b>1.21.11</b>.</li><li>Fabric Loader <b>0.20.1 or newer</b> and Fabric API for the same Minecraft version.</li><li><b>Java 21</b>.</li><li>The Larp Client JAR, available through private access.</li></ul><h2 id="install">Install in four steps</h2><ol class="steps-doc"><li><b>Request access</b>Message iTake using the <a href="/#access">access section</a>. There is no public client download on this website.</li><li><b>Set up Fabric</b>Install Fabric for Minecraft 1.21.11 in your preferred launcher.</li><li><b>Add the mods</b>Place Fabric API and <code>larp-client-0.14.1.jar</code> in the instance’s <code>mods</code> folder.</li><li><b>Launch and customize</b>Start the Fabric instance. Open Larp with <kbd>Right Shift</kbd> or from the title screen.</li></ol><h2 id="update">Updating an existing instance</h2><p>Close Minecraft, remove the previous Larp JAR and add the new one. Keep one Larp version in your mods folder. Back up your configuration before making large changes.</p><h2 id="platforms">Desktop media features</h2><p>Music Player uses Windows media controls. Recorder, Instant Replay desktop audio and Music Beats use Windows-specific capture paths. Do not assume these features work on macOS or Linux.</p><h2 id="support">Something did not start?</h2><p>Check the Minecraft version, Fabric API and Java version first. Then see <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>.</p>''',
'client-menu':'''<h2 id="open">Open your setup</h2><p>Press <kbd>Right Shift</kbd> or choose Larp Client on the title screen. Browse HUD, PvP, Utility, Visuals and Cosmetics, or open the dedicated Kill Efects section.</p><h2 id="new">What changed</h2><ul><li>Emblem-focused home screen with a player preview, your last server and current music.</li><li>A shared dark line background in out-of-world menus; in a world, menus can leave the game visible behind them.</li><li>Custom accent selection and directly editable text fields.</li><li>Profile deletion, reset confirmation and animated notifications.</li></ul><h2 id="language">English and Spanish</h2><p>Hover the thin bar at the bottom of the title screen to reveal the language selector. Move away to close it. The client supports English and Spanish.</p><h2 id="settings">Changing settings</h2><p>Open a module’s options to adjust its behavior. NEW badges identify recent additions. You can use the search field to find a module quickly.</p>''',
'keybinds':'''<h2 id="defaults">Useful default keys</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Default</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Open client menu</td><td>Right Shift</td><td>Rebind in Minecraft Controls.</td></tr><tr><td>Save a 30-second clip</td><td>F8</td><td>Enable Instant Replay and wait for its buffer.</td></tr><tr><td>Show shulker contents</td><td>Left Shift</td><td>Hover a shulker; Shulker Preview must be enabled.</td></tr><tr><td>Take a screenshot</td><td>F2</td><td>Uses Minecraft’s screenshot key.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="customize">Choose your own keys</h2><p>Go to Options → Controls → Key Binds → Larp Client. Module toggle binds, the clip key and shulker preview key are configurable. Check for conflicts if an action does not respond.</p>''',
'macros':'''<h2 id="create">Create a macro</h2><p>Open Macros, choose New macro, select a trigger and type a command such as <code>/spawn</code> or a chat message. A slash sends a command.</p><h2 id="triggers">Keys and actions</h2><p>Macros can use key presses or supported event triggers such as a player kill, death and joining a world. Choose the action in the macro menu instead of assigning every macro a key.</p><p>Example: a kill-triggered macro can send <code>/spawn</code> after a qualifying player kill. Event detection depends on the information the server sends to the client.</p><h2 id="storage">Keep control of automation</h2><p>Edit or delete macros in the same menu. Macros are stored in <code>config/larpclient-macros.json</code>. Use commands and automation only where the server allows them; avoid repeated chat spam.</p>''',
'discord-rpc':'''<h2 id="enable">A built-in presence</h2><p>Enable Discord RPC to show Larp Client, your server, Minecraft version and elapsed session time on Discord. The application identity and logo are already included in the client.</p><div class="callout tip"><p>You no longer need to create a Discord application, paste an Application ID or upload the logo to get started.</p></div><h2 id="privacy">Choose what you share</h2><p>The module includes options for showing the server IP, game version, elapsed time and other status details. Review these before sharing your session.</p><h2 id="buttons">Status buttons</h2><p>Configure the available button labels and HTTPS links in the module’s options. Discord does not let you click your own presence buttons; other people can see and use them.</p><h2 id="missing">If the status does not appear</h2><p>Run the Discord desktop app, check the module is enabled and check Discord’s activity visibility settings. If another app publishes a conflicting presence, try disabling that other presence.</p>''',
'music-player':'''<h2 id="source">Your music, alongside your game</h2><p>Music Player reads the active Windows media session to display a track title, artist, artwork and progress. Controls depend on what the media application exposes to Windows.</p><h2 id="artwork">Artwork and fallback</h2><p>The client uses the track artwork when available. If a cover is delayed or missing, it can display the Larp emblem while waiting.</p><h2 id="control">Playback controls</h2><p>Use the player’s previous, play/pause and next controls when the chat is open, or assign media shortcuts in Minecraft Controls.</p><h2 id="more">Make music part of the scene</h2><p><a href="/docs/lyrics">Lyrics</a> adds LRCLIB text to the world or HUD. Music Beats visualizes desktop audio around your player. Desktop media integration requires Windows.</p><h2 id="trouble">No track or cover?</h2><p>Start a track in your media app and confirm it is exposed to Windows media controls. If needed, inspect <code>%TEMP%\\larp_media_log.txt</code> before asking for help.</p>''',
'profiles':'''<h2 id="slots">Keep different setups</h2><p>Open Client Settings → Profiles. The three profile slots let you save a configuration and load it later. Each populated slot can also be deleted.</p><h2 id="reset">A fresh start</h2><p>The reset category in Client Settings restores the configuration after a confirmation. Accept to apply the reset and show a notification, or cancel to close the confirmation without resetting.</p><h2 id="personalize">Small details, your way</h2><p>Use the custom color button to choose an accent beyond the presets. Text fields can be edited directly; Clear removes the value and Paste inserts clipboard text.</p><h2 id="files">Configuration files</h2><ul><li><code>config/larpclient.json</code> — active configuration.</li><li><code>config/larpclient-profile-1.json</code> through <code>-3</code> — saved profiles.</li><li><code>config/larpclient-waypoints.json</code> — waypoints.</li><li><code>config/larpclient-macros.json</code> — macros.</li></ul><p>Recorder and Instant Replay stay off when a profile is loaded; start capture explicitly.</p>''',
'performance':'''<h2 id="monitor">NEW: Performance Monitor</h2><p>Enable HUD → Performance Monitor for frame times, FPS, 1% lows, P95 and memory use. These describe your current session; the website’s sample graph is illustrative.</p><h2 id="profiling">Optional module profiling</h2><p>Profile module ticks measures the CPU cost of module tick handlers and highlights the most expensive one. It does not measure GPU work or all module rendering. Profiling starts off to avoid unnecessary work.</p><h2 id="renderer">Rendering improvements</h2><p>Recent revisions reduce repeated allocations with streamed geometry, cached trigonometry and reusable cosmetic topology. Rounded shapes no longer need opaque corner masks. Cosmetics reuse prepared data instead of rebuilding everything on every frame.</p><h2 id="capture">Capture has a budget</h2><p>Frame capture uses a small reusable buffer pool. Instant Replay keeps compressed video segments and a fixed-size audio history. Only one clip export can be pending; export happens outside the render thread.</p><h2 id="tune">Find your balance</h2><ul><li>Enable effects gradually and compare frame times in the same scene.</li><li>Lower cosmetic refresh rates or effect counts if your setup needs it.</li><li>Disable recording and replay when you are not using them.</li><li>Be mindful of blur, shaders, resolution and enabled visual effects.</li></ul><p>No fixed FPS increase is guaranteed. Hardware, worlds and other mods affect the result. Automated tests are not a replacement for checking a real Windows gameplay session.</p>''',
'faq':'''<h2 id="access">Is Larp public?</h2><p>Not yet. It is private and in active development. <a href="/#access">Request access from iTake</a>.</p><h2 id="launcher">Is this a launcher?</h2><p>No. Larp is a Fabric mod that goes into an existing Minecraft 1.21.11 instance.</p><h2 id="rules">Can I use it on every server?</h2><p>Servers set their own rules. Check those rules for visual modifications, macros and any other modules you enable.</p><h2 id="cosmetics">Do others see my cosmetics?</h2><p>Cosmetics are rendered locally on your screen.</p><h2 id="audio">Do clips have audio?</h2><p>Yes, since 0.14.1. Instant Replay captures Windows desktop output with the video; it does not capture the microphone.</p><h2 id="fullscreen">What about F11?</h2><p>Recorder and Instant Replay capture Minecraft’s framebuffer rather than a desktop window rectangle. They use the same capture route in windowed and F11 modes. Check the resulting recordings on your hardware.</p><h2 id="cost">Does this guarantee better FPS?</h2><p>No. The renderer and capture paths use bounded resources and caching, but enabled effects and hardware still determine performance.</p><h2 id="demo">What are the interactive website previews?</h2><p>Lightweight browser demonstrations. They show the concepts and actual cosmetic assets without running Minecraft or modifying your client.</p>''',
'changelog':'''<h2 id="v0141">0.14.1 · Sound for your moments</h2><ul><li>Desktop audio in manual and automatic 30-second clips.</li><li>Timestamped stereo audio history and joint audio/video trimming.</li><li>AAC audio in exported MP4 files.</li><li>Clear notifications if desktop capture is unavailable.</li></ul><h2 id="v0140">0.14.0 · A closer look</h2><ul><li>NEW: Performance Monitor with frame-time graph, 1% lows, P95 and memory.</li><li>NEW: Instant Replay, a rolling 30-second video buffer with a configurable save key and automatic kill clips.</li><li>NEW: In-menu previews for Kill Efects.</li></ul><h2 id="v013">0.13.x · Expression and refinement</h2><ul><li>A dedicated Kill Efects section with exclusive Tralalero and Samurai animations.</li><li>Cached and streamed geometry, fewer allocations and bounded capture/export paths.</li><li>Shulker Preview, Item Details, Inventory Alert, Light Meter and expanded Lyrics options.</li><li>Recorder capture improvements, including the framebuffer path for F11.</li><li>Updated Discord application identity, already built in.</li></ul><h2 id="interface">Menu and quality-of-life improvements</h2><ul><li>Emblem-focused title screen, player pose and shared out-of-world backgrounds.</li><li>Server and music artwork with Larp fallback images.</li><li>Profile deletion and a confirmed configuration reset.</li><li>Direct text editing, custom accent selection and Clear/Paste feedback.</li><li>Numbered screenshots, animated previews, event macros and English/Spanish selection.</li></ul><p>Some changes originated in earlier development builds. These notes group the current release line rather than asserting exact dates for every change.</p>''',
'credits':'''<h2 id="projects">Built with and inspired by</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fabric</td><td>Minecraft mod loader and API.</td></tr><tr><td>Clarity</td><td>Imported visual modules and parts of the 3D effects system. CC0.</td></tr><tr><td>Material Icons</td><td>Icons used by the client and website. Apache 2.0.</td></tr><tr><td>Inter</td><td>Local UI font. SIL Open Font License.</td></tr><tr><td>LRCLIB</td><td>Lyrics metadata and synchronized text.</td></tr><tr><td>FFmpeg</td><td>Capture encoding and MP4 export. See the client’s bundled FFmpeg license notice.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="website">Website imagery</h2><p>The gameplay screenshots were supplied by iTake. Cosmetic renders come from the supplied Larp website assets. Lyrics text in the web demo is original illustrative copy, not song lyrics.</p><p>Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang AB. Larp Client is not affiliated with Mojang or Microsoft.</p>''',
}
NEW_PAGES=[
('instant-replay','Instant Replay','play','Keep the last 30 seconds, including desktop audio.', '''<h2 id="enable">Start your replay buffer</h2><p>On Windows, enable Utility → Instant Replay. Wait at least 30 seconds for the rolling buffer to warm up. Capture is off by default and is not restored automatically from a profile.</p><h2 id="save">Save a moment</h2><ul><li>Press <kbd>F8</kbd> to save a clip. Rebind Save last 30 seconds in Minecraft Controls if needed.</li><li>Enable Save on player kill for automatic clips after qualifying player kills.</li><li>Clips are named <code>Clip-N.mp4</code> and appear in the recordings folder and Recordings gallery.</li></ul><h2 id="sound">Game audio and music</h2><p>Version 0.14.1 captures stereo audio from Windows’ default output device, including game audio and music using that device. It does not capture your microphone. Missing audio packets are kept as silence so later sound does not shift forward.</p><h2 id="limits">A deliberately bounded buffer</h2><p>Capture is up to 720p at 30 FPS. The client retains roughly 33 compressed video segments and 40 seconds of PCM audio. At 48 kHz, the audio history is about 7.3 MiB. Clip export uses AAC audio and runs in the background.</p><p>There is one pending export at a time and at least 10 seconds between requests. The video buffer stops if it exceeds its 256 MiB storage limit.</p><h2 id="exclusive">Recorder and Replay</h2><p>Recorder and Instant Replay are mutually exclusive because they share the capture path. Stop one before enabling the other. Disabling Replay stops audio capture and removes its temporary buffer.</p><h2 id="troubleshoot">If a clip cannot be saved</h2><p>Check the warm-up notice, your default Windows audio device, free disk space and the capture module state. Audio initialization failure is reported instead of silently saving a muted clip.</p>'''),
('kill-effects','Kill Efects','hitfx','One final hit. One chosen animation.', '''<h2 id="choose">Choose one animation</h2><p>Open the dedicated Kill Efects section and choose <b>Tralalero</b> or <b>Samurai</b>. The selection is exclusive: only the chosen animation runs after a qualifying player kill.</p><h2 id="tralalero">Tralalero</h2><p>A stylized shark in blue sneakers enters the scene and swallows the defeated player. The client renders the effect locally.</p><h2 id="samurai">Samurai</h2><p>A slicing effect separates the player body into textured fragments. The body fragments use prepared geometry to limit repeated work.</p><h2 id="preview">Preview before playing</h2><p>Choose Preview in the Kill Efects menu to watch the animation on a mannequin using your skin. Close preview hides it without changing your selection or enabling an effect in the world.</p><h2 id="options">Make it fit your setup</h2><p>Options include scale, opacity, duration, effect refresh rate and an Only my kills trigger. The browser’s stylized animation is an illustration; the client uses its own 3D renderer.</p>'''),
('lyrics','Lyrics','music','Bring the words into your world.', '''<h2 id="source">Powered by LRCLIB</h2><p>Lyrics uses track information from the Windows media session to retrieve lyrics from LRCLIB. Availability and synchronized timing depend on the song’s metadata and what LRCLIB has for that recording.</p><h2 id="placement">Three placements</h2><ul><li><b>World:</b> place the current phrase in the world, fixed per line or following the player.</li><li><b>HUD:</b> a movable lyrics widget.</li><li><b>Compact:</b> a single-line style, including an option above the music player.</li></ul><h2 id="style">Make the text yours</h2><p>Adjust size, width, line layout, line spacing, color and animation speed. Font choices include Inter (iOS), Inter Bold (iOS), Montserrat and Minecraft. Text effects include Fade, Slide, Glow and None.</p><h2 id="timing">Timing and paused playback</h2><p>Use Sync offset in milliseconds to fine-tune the line timing. Hide when paused controls whether the lyric remains visible after playback stops. Unsynchronized lyrics do not provide automatic word-level karaoke timing.</p><h2 id="missing">No lyrics found?</h2><p>Check that the media session reports the right song and artist. Some songs, alternate recordings and instrumental tracks have no matching lyric entry.</p>'''),
('shulker-preview','Shulker Preview','inventoryhud','Look inside without opening the box.', '''<h2 id="show">Preview the contents</h2><p>Enable Utility → Shulker Preview, hover a shulker box in an inventory and hold the preview key. The default is <kbd>Left Shift</kbd>. The tooltip can show all 27 slots and item counts.</p><h2 id="key">Choose your key</h2><p>Rebind the shulker contents action in Options → Controls → Larp Client. Always show preview removes the need to hold the key.</p><h2 id="color">Match the box</h2><p>Enable Match shulker color to tint the preview using the shulker’s dye color. White shulkers use white; blue shulkers use blue. Disable it to use a neutral background.</p><h2 id="data">About the contents</h2><p>The preview uses the container data attached to the item stack. It is an inventory convenience, not a tool for discovering unseen containers or server-side data.</p>'''),
('captures','Screenshots & Recorder','camera','Keep a screenshot or record a whole session.', '''<h2 id="screenshots">Screenshots</h2><p>Take a screenshot with Minecraft’s screenshot key, normally <kbd>F2</kbd>. The client uses numbered <code>ScreenShot-N</code> names, an animated preview and chat actions for copying and previewing the result.</p><h2 id="recorder">Recorder</h2><p>Enable Recorder for an ongoing recording. Options include frame rate, resolution, encoder, quality and desktop audio. Windows capture reads the Minecraft framebuffer, so windowed and F11 modes use the same capture path.</p><h2 id="gallery">Your recordings</h2><p>Use the Recordings button to browse captures and clips. Recorder is for a recording you explicitly start and stop; <a href="/docs/instant-replay">Instant Replay</a> keeps a rolling 30-second history.</p><h2 id="audio">Audio and resource use</h2><p>Desktop audio uses the default Windows output device. Recorder and Replay cannot be active together. Enable capture only when needed, and check the saved file before relying on a recording.</p>'''),
]
